[Music]  in the 3rd century bc  greek scientist eratosthenes was the  first to calculate the circumference of  our planet by measuring the length of  shadows in two different cities  at the same time of day proving that the  world we live in is  indeed spherical rather than a flat  plain however  it wouldn't be until 1967 that the first  colored picture of the earth in its  entirety was made by the american ats-3  satellite  which makes me think what about the  fantasy world of zelda  although it has very little impact on  the story beats of the series  as someone with a keen interest in  astronomy i've always secretly wondered  what this world in its entirety would  look like  every game in the series takes place in  its own confined area of land and maps  provided by the game will show how said  land is laid out  but we've never been given an accurate  depiction of the world as a whole  the closest we get is fan art made by  zelda enthusiasts who attempted to  sketch an overall idea  but nothing official from nintendo  themselves has ever been published  so is hyrule a planet well  yes and no if you were to ask if hyrule  is located on the planet then  yes but if the question is is the planet  named hyrule  then no hyrule is just a stretch of land  among many  a kingdom which has expanded contracted  and relocated  many times throughout zelda's history  it's understandable that some might  confuse hyrule as the name of the planet  since some of the wording in the  creation story seems to hint at this  stating things such as the goddesses  descended onto the chaos that was  hyrule but there is a simple explanation  for this the creation myth as presented  is always told from the vantage point of  beings who live  in and around hyrule it's not uncommon  for tales of creation to be centered  around the culture  and land from which it originated in the  japanese shinto creation story  japan is the first landmass to be  created similarly the ancient greeks and  romans too had stories revolving around  gods creating and settling  unrecognizable landmarks within their  own territory such as crete and mount  olympus  in turn placing themselves and their  land at the heart of the creation story  as such it's easy to believe that the  hylians and other inhabitants of the  kingdom pass on the stories of creation  in a way that it places them  at the center of it all after all in  their eyes hyrule is the superior  kingdom chosen by the gods in reality  the gods created so much more than just  the land of hyrule  but how do we know for sure that hyrule  is located on a planet and not some flat  plain floating around in a void  or some sort of magic snow globe well  first off we have the presence of the  sun and moon  two celestial bodies we are all too  familiar with if the moon is a sphere it  only makes sense that the world itself  is two as per the laws of gravity unless  you want to join the flat earth society  who don't believe in a round earth but  do acknowledge that mars is a sphere  alrighty then  we also see stars in the sky and other  traits one would find on a planet like  our own such as sunrise and sunset  seasons plate tectonics and even  specific weather events such as storms  are only possible on a spherical world  but these are all scientific  explanations something the developers  could have easily just  copied from our own world since these  are things that are familiar to us  after all without gravity the games  would be  very different in general it's no use  comparing the gravity from the zelda  series to  those of our own world one because the  strength of gravity isn't universal and  slightly varies between titles depending  on the engine  and two because most games generally  simulate something close to earth's  gravity  even those that don't take place on  earth  however there is actual in-game evidence  feign's witch directly hint at the  existence of a planet  on which the series takes place for  instance the presence of globes  inside tetra's cabin aboard her pirate  ship we find what seems to be a full  representation of the planet  we also find a stranger variant of a  globe inside the astral observatory in  majora's mask  as well as a research note plastered on  the wall which seems to depict a green  planet  with the moon orbiting around it so yes  the events of the zelda series most  likely take place on a planet  but then what is its name well as boring  as it might sound  earth throughout the series the word  earth is used on many different  occasions to describe the world as a  whole  we also have an interview with siri's  former and current producers  shigeru miyamoto and aeginuma in which  they state this fact  so the land's hyrule what's the planet  called  although this interview is definitely  humoristic and playful in nature  do notice how miyamoto is very quick and  resolute in his reaction  he's been the producer of the series  since its inception  and set most of the standards for the  series back in the day  until the baton was passed to enuma  hence many of the series tropes  including the first bits of the overall  lore originated from him  this begs the question though if this is  earth is it  our earth well again yes and no in a way  this  is indeed the same planet we inhabit  however it's not set in our timeline or  even our reality if this confuses you i  think tolkien said it best when he was  asked  a similar question about his fantasy  world most people have made this mistake  anything in middle earth is a particular  kind of earth or is another planet and  you know in the science fiction song but  it's simply an old-fashioned word for  the  for this world we live in as imagined  surrounded by the ocean  it seemed to me that that middle earth  was was in a sense as you say  this world we live in but um this world  we live in at a different era  no at a different stage of imagination  but you make no attempt at all to tie  this up with time as we know it today  why is this because it had been  impossible  it won't really work out you know either  paleontologically or archaeologically at  all actually  i mean then you can't really relate the  landmasses i described them  satisfactorily to the landmasses we know  now  as tolkien states it is indeed our  planet it is earth  in a different state of imagination and  this too seems to apply to the fantasy  world of zelda  some games do establish that it takes  place in our reality  they loosely follow real-life events  such as wars or other significant parts  of our history  others take place far far into the  future when mankind is much more  advanced  yet other games like fallout have a bit  of both everything leading up to its  prologue is based on our timeline but  then it veers off into its own reality  one in which nuclear power was fully  embraced after the second world war  resulting in an alternate version of the  1950s where technology is way more  advanced than it was in real life  but in the zelda series there's nothing  that suggests that it's supposed to take  place in our own reality  it seems to follow its own timeline and  history and even in the technology  department it's  all over the place on the one hand we  see technology which reflects those from  medieval times  on the other hand we see things that far  outshine our current day advancements  the zelda series also doesn't seem to  bother much with keeping track of  actual dates everything is categorized  in eras like the era of the sky  or the era of light and dark and so on  and in a lot of cases these eras  are separated by huge amounts of time  often indicated by  ages or eons so there's no real way of  telling when a game takes place  all we can determine is the order  there's only one game which  actually mentions a specific date which  is the wind waker on windfall island we  can find a tombstone with hylian text on  it the translation of which tells us  that a great artist is buried here  accompanied by a year of birth and death  831-894 of course it's impossible to  deduce anything from this  the wind waker is set to take place only  about a hundred years after ocarina of  time but we have no idea when the  hylians started keeping count and it's  obvious that it doesn't encompass the  zelda timeline as a whole as skyward  sword and minish cap alone already take  place many ages apart  definitely a lot longer than 800 years  it's a bit similar to how our current  day calendar only started counting a  little over two millennia ago but it is  at least  interesting to see an actual date pop up  in the zelda timeline  but let's get back to the planet itself  which as we established is called earth  and is in fact based on our earth and we  have plenty of evidence for this  if this was just some far-off planet in  a galaxy far far away  it likely wouldn't have been called  earth first of all  the sun and moon would have had  different names as well the sun  or soul is simply the name of our home  star  and the moon or luna the name of the  companion orbiting us  so far people have been able to match at  least three familiar constellations in  various games which all match  exactly with those from our real world  orion  big dipper and cassiopeia if hyrule's  planet was an alien planet  either in a different part of the milky  way or even a different galaxy  altogether  the presence of these constellations  would be impossible  though the stars in the sky appear as a  two-dimensional plane or dome wrapped  around the earth  the actual distance between each  individual star is vastly different  the patterns we've laid out for them  only work from the vantage point  of our planet move to a different point  in space and the alignments would no  longer be the same  if zelda had its own made-up  constellations this wouldn't have been  an issue  but a celestial pattern such as a famous  big dipper would only be visible from  the vantage point  of our planet more interestingly  constellations seem to be  of more importance in the zelda universe  than just a decorative reference  to our own world stargazing and  celestial patterns  are recurring theme in the zelda series  in the wind waker a picture of orion can  be found inside tetris cabin right next  to the globe we mentioned earlier  we also find three islands with patterns  matching that of the three  constellations we  previously listed in majora's mask an  astral observatory stands in the central  fields of termina  its occupant professor shakashi doing  vigorous research into the night sky  notes of celestial bodies strange  otherworldly crystals  and other curiosities scattered around  the floor and walls of the observatory  in twilight princess we can clearly  observe the recognizable three-star belt  of orion in the night sky  and this obsession with celestial  alignments was taken to the extreme in  2017's breath of the wild  although there are no constellations  visible in the night sky this time  around they do play a prominent role in  the game's lore  particularly that of the ancient chica  and their mysterious technology  constellations are found all over their  machines in architecture  most notably the star map inside the  giant dome-shaped room inside hyrule  castle  which is confirmed to be an astral  observatory we also find  giant shika telescopes used to study the  night skies at the two main laboratories  above ground  as of right now it remains a mystery why  these constellations are so  important to the sheikah though there  are plenty of theories  it has never been confirmed why nintendo  has such a specific interest in orion  the big dipper and cassiopeia  it's definitely a reoccurring thing they  keep putting in on purpose but there are  some real-life  ancient legends and customs which might  explain their inclusion  the big dipper is the easiest to explain  as it has an interesting meaning in  various asian cultures  in shintoism the big dipper which  consists of seven stars represents the  seven divine generations of kami  however even more on the nose is its  meaning in indian astronomy  here the big dipper was initially called  the bear but was later more commonly  known by the name of sapterishi  or seven sages hence it could very well  be possible that the inclusion of the  big dipper is meant to symbolize the  famous seven sages of hylian legends  orion is a bit harder to pinpoint in  terms of its meaning or symbolism as it  has many different meanings especially  in japanese mythology but it is a  constellation that plays some degree of  importance in both shinto  and buddhist traditions and is closely  tied to either music  ancestral spirits or specific deities  but if the fact that tetra has this  constellation in particular framed on  her desk has any deeper meaning is  unclear at this point cassiopeia is very  interesting when put into context with  the game it's most prominently featured  in that being the wind waker  cassiopeia was a queen in ancient greek  mythology according to legend she  angered poseidon the god of the sea  who then sent a sea monster cetus to  ravage the kingdom  given the wind waker's theme of a  kingdom ravaged and swallowed up by the  sea  it couldn't be more fitting to have this  constellation make its appearance here  all the myths and symbolism aside it  could also be that nintendo included  these three constellations in particular  because they are generally well known  throughout all cultures  in breath of the wild we find another  common trait of that of a planet  that being these enormous craters likely  caused by meteorite impacts on the  surface of hyrule  meteors of course being rocks who  originate from the vacuum of space  as well as star fragments basically  small glassy meteorites raining down  from space and onto hyrule's landscape  since the evidence suggests that hyrule  is indeed a planet with a moon and  orbiting a star  aka the sun one would assume based on  our real life experience  that it is part of a larger solar system  in other words  are there other worlds out there as well  the short answer is likely  yes there are some small hints which  indicate the presence of other planets  one of these being two research notes  found on the floor of the astral  observatory in majora's mask  although very crude they seem to depict  a solar system with various celestial  bodies orbiting around a center point  this could be proof that indeed other  planets exist out there  second is the existence of well  aliens yes unlike our real world the  zelda universe has  undeniable proof of alien visitation  there have been quite some videos and  theories about the strange ghostly  entities visiting romani ranch  only known as them or they speculations  surrounding these otherworldly beings  have attempted to write them off as  simply  ghosts or some other earthly or magical  phenomena  but time and time again the evidence  heavily leans towards actual alien  visitors  from the creature they were based on  that being a real-life alien encounter  from west virginia  to quotes from the game's producer ag  onuma to photographs of  ufos not to mention the fact that it has  all the tropes of classic american  abduction stories involving either cows  and even people getting snatched up by  aliens  and there is one more interesting piece  of evidence that hints to these  creatures originating from the skies  above  those who are familiar with the side  quest know that the alien attack on the  ranch takes place on the first night of  majora's three-day cycle  if we look to the sky on the night of  the first day we can see a red star  right above the big dipper constellation  at first people speculated that this  might be beetlejuice  a giant star 700 times bigger than our  own sun  which is part of the orion constellation  this star can actually be seen glowing  red  even with the naked eye however as  mentioned before the red star in  majora's mask is located right above the  big dipper  not orion more interestingly however  on the second and third night the star  is  gone it disappears from the night sky  this coincides with the alien attack on  the first night  after which they take off and are never  seen again  if these are indeed aliens which the  evidence seems to suggest  this means that they had to have  originated from another planet out there  somewhere  of course aside from the singular  encounter the possible presence of other  planets has little to no bearings on the  overarching story events of the zelda  series as a whole  at least not right now however it does  open the door to future possibilities  we've seen from breath of the wild  concept art that nintendo has been  toying around the idea of aliens being  the main threat to hyrule and its heroes  and although this concept was ultimately  scrapped who is to say that this won't  become a reality in the future  perhaps they might even go as far as to  have us visit  one or more of these alien worlds who  knows  until then we can only imagine  one final thing to address is the  radical changes in hyrule's geography  between each installment  in my opinion there's two valid  explanations for this  well three actually the first is the  most likely and also  the most boring one since it's more  grounded in reality and that is that  nintendo simply  doesn't care about consistency and  values gameplay above  anything else after all exploring the  exact same hyrule every time would get  boring after so many games  the second one is that the landscape  changes from game to game due to all  kinds of natural factors like plate  tectonics  catastrophic events and generally just  nature being nature  i've attempted to piece this together in  my evolution of hyrule series with a  mild level of success but there were  many things which were very hard or even  impossible to explain or at least  required severely stretching it  ultimately i even had to give up on some  games because the changes were simply  too radical  but the evolution series was never  intended to find a solid explanation for  everything and was more or less a  thought experiment to see how far we  could get in coming up with reasons why  which is where the third explanation  comes in there is a much more elegant  and simple solution for this phenomena  without mentioning game design or  trying to explain every individual  change in hyrule's landmarks  and the solution is hidden in the title  of the series  the legend of zelda the idea is that  every game in the series is a distant  legend that you  the player experienced as if it was  being retold by someone  and as is with all legends and ancient  myths the accounts and details of what  happened and how the landscape looked  exactly  quickly blurs over time lost in  translation through the many retellings  of set's story  we don't actually need to explain why a  forest is here and then all of a sudden  here in the next game all that matters  is that there was a forest called  the lost wood somewhere and that some  significant events took place here  this approach essentially solves any  inconsistency the theory has when it  comes to its geography  there is even more to mention about the  world of zelda as everything i've  described here is within the scope of  the quote-unquote normal world  also referred to as the world of light  or light world but  as many of you know the zelda series is  rife with alternate dimensions or realms  many of which are almost impossible to  pinpoint where exactly these could be  located relative to hyrule there's also  a lot of conflicting information about  which lands are parallel dimensions and  which are not  and to this day we still have no clear  understanding of what termina  actually is if it's a completely  different reality on a different plane  of existence or if it's simply located  somewhere else on the planet but still  on the same physical plane as hyrule  as such different realms are best saved  for a future video as they are a whole  other topic altogether  i hope you enjoyed this deep dive into  the universe of the legend of zelda and  i hope to see you in the next video  first off a big thanks to nintendo black  crisis for once again being my partner  in crime for this one he'll be releasing  his own video next week so be sure to  check it out when it's ready  i'll put a link to it in the description  as soon as it's up and of course a  massive thanks as always goes to my  supporters right here on youtube  and on patreon you guys are the best oh  and please say hello to sakamoto  shinonome for joining my patreon crew  and to perry of hyrule who finally  decided to become a member thank you  perry  it is greatly appreciated and that is  all for now  this is don signing off and have a good  [Music]  [Music]  one  [Music]  you

